The module demonstrated how custom routing enhances network security.

Step 6: Understanding Network Virtual Appliances (NVAs)

A major focus of the module was Network Virtual Appliances.

An NVA is a virtual machine that performs network-related functions.

Common NVA functions:
Firewall
Intrusion Detection System (IDS)
Intrusion Prevention System (IPS)
Traffic inspection
Routing services
Proxy services
Examples:
Cisco Firepower
Palo Alto Networks Firewall
Fortinet FortiGate
Custom Linux routing appliances
Benefits:
Advanced traffic control
Security inspection
Centralized policy enforcement

The module emphasized that NVAs are commonly used in enterprise cloud environments.

